{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfevYa9bZYHkh1LpLPJPg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 08 is done: the first full LaTeX draft of paper 2 is in `paper2/latex/`. It builds with `make` to **24 pages**, with no undefined references or citations and no overfull boxes. The gate passes: lake build ok, the one `sorry` is the §24 conjecture, MOSP pytest 1,407 passed, pathwidth_solver pytest 114 passed.\n\n**Template: still to obtain.** INFORMS's author pages refused scripted access (HTTP 403), including through the web fetch tool. So the draft uses the `article` class, and I could not read the journal's formatting rules either; the layout is a stand-in. Someone needs to download the class by hand, then switch the document class and the bibliography style.\n\n**What's in it**\n- **Sections 1 and 5** are marked placeholders. Section 1 also has a draft list of contributions and the notation.\n- **Section 2** has the method paragraph, the check against a second labelling rule, Table 2.1 and the three print figures.\n- **Section 3** has:\n  - the twelve problems, each stated precisely;\n  - the master table;\n  - the Helly and clique lemmas, with proofs of vs = pw and Z = pw + 1;\n  - the exact core, the two bands, the two false rows and the edge cases;\n  - the Kirousis & Papadimitriou proof gap, and pebbling.\n- **Section 4**:\n  - The counterexample is **Figure 4.1**. The paper numbers it Counterexample 4.4, not 4.5 as in the markdown.\n  - The repair's soundness is credited to Tamaki and Kitsunai et al.\n  - Chu's Theorem 6.3.6 is described as \"reworded\", and re-certification is given as \"112 of 115, 3 in flight\".\n  - The section also covers the cost of the repair, the certificates and the dataset.\n  - Every theorem has its Lean names in a footnote; all 89 names exist.\n- **Tables** come from the CSVs via `python -m paper2.latex.make_tables`, and each matches its recorded table. The exception is the re-certification table, which reads the split run's files live: at 08:18, four refuted and three in flight. Rerun `make tables && make` before quoting it. The master table and the two pathwidth tables of section 4 were written by hand from the source documents.\n- **Bibliography.** `refs.bib` has 44 entries: `table1.bib` with its notes dropped, plus 31 more. All 36 DOIs were checked against Crossref or DataCite, with three registry quirks accepted and their reasons recorded. Priem et al. (2022) was checked against arXiv 2205.01833. Entries without a DOI were checked against the PDFs we hold.\n\n**Gaps in the draft**\n- Bienstock & Seymour (1991) and LaPaugh (1993) are cited but not held.\n- The deficiency form of Hall's theorem is used without a citation, because Ore (1955) is not held.\n- The equivalence-chain figure is left out: at text width its labels would be about 2.5 pt.\n- natbib labels Yanasse's EJOR paper \"1997a\" and the Pesquisa Operacional paper \"1997b\", the reverse of the project's names.\n\n**Also added:** `check_refs.py`, `check_lean.py` and 5 tests in `tests/test_paper2_latex.py`; a README in `paper2/latex/`; and a pointer in `plan.md`.\n\nThe split run is clean: no `!!!` line, and the process is alive. The item is marked `[x]` and PROGRESS.md now reads 8/9; item 09 (the reserve) remains, so no LOOP_COMPLETE."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":350111,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":439,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":741,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7884aff6-aa71-4f85-a709-a301fa2453ad","uuid":"2e5dedd9-a5d3-4ba7-933f-03cf254ba914","timestamp":"2026-10-03T07:39:47.635Z","request_id":"req_011CfevYZgpFKKzNEACUo55S"}
